All six features implemented and verified. Here's the summary of changes:

### `app/auth.py` — Authentication
- `require_api_key` reads the `X-API-Key` header, looks it up in `VALID_API_KEYS`, returns the username on match, raises **HTTP 401** on missing or invalid key.

### `app/main.py` — Endpoints

| Endpoint | Changes |
|---|---|
| `GET /tasks` | Added optional `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to` filters (combinable, any subset). Added `page` (default 1) and `page_size` (default 20, max 100) pagination. |
| `POST /tasks` | Requires auth. Validates `project_id` exists (404 if not). Auto-generates `id = max(existing) + 1`. Returns 201. |
| `PUT /tasks/{task_id}` | Requires auth. Partial update via `exclude_unset=True` — only sent fields change. Returns 404 if not found. |
| `DELETE /tasks/{task_id}` | Requires auth. Returns 204 on success, 404 if not found. |

### Verified (13/13 passed)
All tested against the running server: auth guards (401 on missing/bad key), project validation (404), create (201 with auto-ID), partial update (200, only specified fields change), delete (204), get by ID, unfiltered list, status filter, pagination, and 404 on nonexistent resources.
